Summary of the Production Strategy 
1.	Transport Layer: Use Netty for your custom Java WebSocket/TCP connection handlers. It handles hundreds of thousands of concurrent clients efficiently via non-blocking I/O (NIO). 
2.	Messaging Spine: Use Apache Kafka partitioned by your ascope schema (areas, structures, communities, organizations, people, events) so independent server clusters process specific slices of the data graph. 
3.	Agentic Control: Build your management layer using LangChain4j, feeding cluster metrics (Prometheus/Grafana telemetry) directly to LLM agents capable of executing scaling instructions across your infrastructure. 



